#
# Counter-example for the math:ParallelTransport frame (issue #1527, Commit E): a
# math:ParallelTransport naming its math:transportConnection rule but omitting its
# math:transportAlong path — transport that goes nowhere. The min-1 qualified restriction on
# math:transportAlong derives a sh:qualifiedMinCount property shape, so validation MUST emit
# shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding
# (math:IncompleteParallelTransport).
# ISOLATION: the math:transportConnection arm is satisfied by a well-formed math:Connection
# (naming its math:connectionOn so math:IncompleteConnection stays silent), so only the
# math:transportAlong arm fires.
# Back-reference: math:IncompleteParallelTransport (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecParallelTransportNoPath).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:transport a math:ParallelTransport ;
    math:transportConnection ex:connection .    # names the rule but NO math:transportAlong

ex:connection a math:Connection ;
    math:connectionOn ex:sheaf .
ex:sheaf a math:CellularSheaf ;
    math:sheafBaseComplex ex:base ;
    math:hasStalk ex:stalk ;
    math:restrictionMap ex:restriction .
ex:base a math:CellComplex .
ex:stalk a math:SheafStalk ; math:stalkOverCell ex:cell .
ex:cell a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:restriction a math:SheafRestrictionMap ; math:sourceObject ex:stalk ; math:targetObject ex:stalk .
